                                          "id":  "ne3-known-issues",
                                          "title":  "Fixed data quality issues (as of today)",
                                          "query":  "### Two fixed data quality issues\n\n1. **Material.recycledContent_pct** carried density values instead of percentages for the 5 generic ILCD/IDEMAT background materials (lead, copper, steel, zinc, aluminium) - the cause was an unescaped comma in the name field during CSV import. Source and live data are now corrected (name quoted correctly, recycledContent_pct is now honestly set to unknown instead of a wrong number).\n2. **ImpactCategory** contained 42 nodes with considerable redundancy from an inconsistent EF3.1 import (e.g. IC_EF_CLIMATE_FOSSIL and IC_EF_CLIMATE_CHANGE_FOSSIL were the same indicator under two IDs). Consolidated to 28 unique categories, all HAS_CATEGORY edges re-pointed, CHARACTERIZES/DECLARES were never affected.",
